This is actually a dangerous way unless you know what you
are doing.  For this to work, you have to be of one alignment,
the altar a second alignment, and the unicorn corpse the third
alignment.  Any other combination will be bad (ie, sacrifice
a unicorn on an altar of the same alignment as the corpse, and
the god gets angry, sacrifice one of your alignment, and you
may well change alignment, which is VERY BAD if you haven't done
your quest yet).

You can sacrifice any fresh corpse not of your race, and have
a chance of converting the altar.  You have a (XL+2)/(XL+7) chance
of success (rn2(8+u.ulevel) > 5).

Sacrificing a corpse of your own race is pretty bad if you're
not chaotic...

If you are not chaotic, you abuse your wisdom, which can 
eventually lead to a decrease in WIS.

The altar becomes chaotic if it wasn't already.

If the altar is chaotic and you aren't, the altar is destroyed.

If you and the altar are chaotic, your luck increases by 2 and
your alignment increases by 5.

If you are not chaotic, your alignment decreases by 5, your
god's anger is increased by 3, you lose one point of WIS, and
luck is decreased by 5.

There is a chance of Yeenoghu or Juiblex being summoned, otherwise
another type of chaotic demon may be summoned.

Unless you are chaotic, you will be scared, can't move for 3 turns,
and the demon is hostile.  If chaotic, the demon will be peaceful.

